# Everything here is excluded from the build context - the tarball Docker sends to
# the daemon before it runs a single instruction.
#
# Without this file the context is roughly 1.4 GB: the 1 GB virtualenv, the 264 MB
# corpus with four .git directories, and the built indexes. Every one of those is
# either rebuilt inside the image or mounted at runtime, so shipping them makes the
# build slow and the image enormous for no benefit.

# Virtualenv - the image installs its own, for Linux
.venv/
venv/

# Corpus and indexes - mounted as a volume at runtime, not baked in.
# Baking them in would also mean rebuilding the image every time you re-ingest.
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/indexes/
qdrant_storage/

# Model weights - downloaded into a named volume on first run so they survive
# rebuilds. Copying them in would add ~500 MB to every layer.
.cache/
models/

# Secrets. The API key is passed as an environment variable at runtime; an image
# with a key baked into a layer is an image that leaks a key.
.env
.env.local

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Git and editors
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Docs and reports - not needed to run the service
reports/
*.md
!README.md
